\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Brief life is here our portion,
\par Brief sorrows, short- lived care;
\par The life that knows no ending,
\par The tearless life, is there.
\par O happy retribution!
\par Short toil, eternal rest;
\par For mortals and for sinners,
\par A mansion with the blest!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. That we should look, poor
\par wanderers,
\par To have our home on high!
\par That worms should seek for
\par dwellings
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Beyond the starry sky!
\par And now we fight the battle,
\par But then shall wear the crown
\par Of full and everlasting
\par And passionless renown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And now we watch and struggle,
\par And now we live in hope,
\par And Zion in her anguish
\par WIth Babylon must cope;
\par But He whom now we trust in
\par Shall then be seen and known,
\par And they that know and see Him
\par Shall have Him for their own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O sweet and blessed country,
\par The home of God's elect!
\par O sweet and blessed country,
\par That eager hearts expert!
\par Jesu, in mercy bring us
\par To that dear land of rest,
\par Who art, with God the Father
\par And Spirit, ever blest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jerusalem the golden,
\par With milk and honey blessed,
\par Beneath thy contemplation
\par Sink heart and voice oppressed.
\par I know not, O I know not,
\par What joys await us there,
\par What radiancy of glory,
\par What bliss beyond compare!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. They stand, those halls of Zion,
\par All jubilant with song,
\par And bright with many an angel
\par And all the martyr throng;
\par The Prince is ever in them,
\par The daylight is serene;
\par The pastures of the blessed
\par Are decked in glorious sheen.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. There is the throne of David,
\par And there, from care released,
\par The shout of them that triumph,
\par The song of them that feast;
\par And they who, with their Leader,
\par Have conquered in the fight,
\par For ever and for ever
\par Are clad in robes of white.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Strive, man, to win that glory;
\par Toil, man, to gain that light;
\par Send hope before to grasp it,
\par Till hope be lost in sight,
\par Exult, O dust and ashes;
\par The Lord shall be thy part:
\par His only, His for ever
\par Thou shalt be, and thou art.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

